#: src/ch02-15-03-thoth.md:3
msgid ""
"[Thoth](https://github.com/FuzzingLabs/thoth) (pronounced \"taut\" or "
"\"toss\") is a security toolkit for Cairo/Starknet. Written in Python 3, it "
"includes analyzers, disassemblers, and decompilers. Thoth is capable of "
"generating call graphs, control-flow graphs (CFG), and data-flow graphs for "
"Sierra files or Cairo/Starknet compilation artifacts. It also features tools "
"like a symbolic execution engine and a symbolic bounded model checker."
msgstr ""

#: src/ch02-15-03-thoth.md:7
msgid ""
"**Remote & Local Analysis**: Works with contracts on Mainnet/Goerli and "
"local compilations."
msgstr ""

#: src/ch02-15-03-thoth.md:8
msgid ""
"**Decompiler**: Transforms assembly into decompiled code using SSA (Static "
"Single Assignment)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ch02-15-03-thoth.md:9
msgid "**Call Flow Analysis**: Generates Call Flow Graphs."
msgstr ""

#: src/ch02-15-03-thoth.md:10
msgid ""
"**Static Analysis**: Conducts various types of analyses (security/"
"optimization/analytics) on contracts."
msgstr ""

#: src/ch02-15-03-thoth.md:11
msgid ""
"**Symbolic Execution**: Finds variable values for specific paths in "
"functions and generates test cases."
msgstr ""

#: src/ch02-15-03-thoth.md:12
msgid ""
"**Data Flow Analysis**: Produces Data Flow Graphs (DFG) for each function."
msgstr ""

#: src/ch02-15-03-thoth.md:13
msgid "**Disassembler**: Converts bytecode to assembly."
