#: src/ch03-01-transactions.md:35
msgid ""
"With Cairo 0, developers sent Cairo Assembly (CASM) code directly to the "
"sequencer. But with the contemporary Cairo version, they send Sierra code to "
"the Sequencer. Breaking it down, Cairo 0 compiled straight to CASM, while "
"the current Cairo version compiles to Sierra, which subsequently compiles to "
"CASM. A crucial difference is that Sierra executions are infallible and "
"always provable, whereas in Cairo 0, transactions could fail. If they did, "
"they became non-provable. The latest Cairo iteration ensures all code "
"compiles to Sierra, making every transaction reliable."
