"(2^{128}) and the version number of the actual transaction type. For "
"example, if the latest version of a `declare` transaction is 2, then a "
"simulated `declare` transaction would have a version number of (2^{128} + "
"2). The same logic applies to other transaction types like `invoke` and "
"`deploy_account`."
